WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.651
Cut the Earth open, and you
would find three layers.

2
00:00:07.871 --> 00:00:11.493
Nobody has ever dug down to see
them. We know from evidence.

3
00:00:11.993 --> 00:00:15.940
Scientists model the inside
of the Earth as three layers.

4
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.015
The crust is the thin, hard,
rocky outside. We live on it.

5
00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:25.483
Under it is the mantle: a very
thick layer of hot, solid rock.

6
00:00:25.703 --> 00:00:31.554
The mantle is most of the Earth. It is
so hot that it can flow, very slowly.

7
00:00:31.774 --> 00:00:35.536
At the centre is the core.
It is metal, not rock.

8
00:00:35.756 --> 00:00:38.821
The core is about as hot
as the surface of the Sun.

9
00:00:39.321 --> 00:00:45.683
Under the crust, rock is so hot that it
melts. Melted rock underground is magma.

10
00:00:45.903 --> 00:00:49.572
Where the crust is broken, magma
pushes up through the crack.

11
00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:53.693
It erupts. Red-hot lava
pours out, with ash and gas.

12
00:00:53.913 --> 00:00:56.839
Lava is magma that has
reached the surface.

13
00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:01.888
The lava cools into new rock. The
mountain grows, with a crater at the top.

14
00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:06.752
Volcanoes are found at breaks in the
crust. That is why they come in lines.

15
00:01:07.252 --> 00:01:12.732
The crust is not one shell. It is
broken into huge pieces called plates.

16
00:01:12.952 --> 00:01:18.525
The plates rest on the hot mantle. They
creep along as fast as your fingernails grow.

17
00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:23.621
Where two plates push against each
other, their edges catch and stick.

18
00:01:23.841 --> 00:01:27.928
The push builds up for years.
Then the edges slip, all at once.

19
00:01:28.148 --> 00:01:31.631
That sudden move is an
earthquake, and the ground shakes.

20
00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:37.424
A crack is left behind. Earthquakes
happen at the same breaks as volcanoes.

21
00:01:37.924 --> 00:01:41.360
How thin is the crust, really?
Imagine the Earth as an apple.

22
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.620
The skin stands for the crust.
The real crust is even thinner.

23
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.834
The flesh is the mantle: most
of the Earth, thick and hot.

24
00:01:50.054 --> 00:01:54.884
The apple's core stands for the
Earth's core, but it is far too small.

25
00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:59.655
No model shows everything. This one
leaves out the heat and the metal.

26
00:02:00.155 --> 00:02:03.777
Nobody has seen the mantle or
the core. So how do we know?

27
00:02:03.997 --> 00:02:09.013
Earthquakes send waves right through the
Earth. Some only travel through solids.

28
00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:12.391
They pass through the mantle,
so the mantle is solid.

29
00:02:12.611 --> 00:02:16.651
They cannot get through the outer
core, so that part is liquid.

30
00:02:16.871 --> 00:02:20.261
The Earth is far too heavy to
be rock all the way through.

31
00:02:20.481 --> 00:02:26.008
And meteorites, rocks from space, are
sometimes made of iron. The core is metal.

32
00:02:26.228 --> 00:02:31.382
Evidence from enquiry built this
model. It changed what people thought.

33
00:02:31.882 --> 00:02:39.127
Crust, mantle, core: thin rock, thick
hot rock, and metal at the centre.

34
00:02:39.347 --> 00:02:42.969
Volcanoes and earthquakes happen
where the crust is broken.

35
00:02:43.189 --> 00:02:46.533
An apple can model that,
and evidence is how we know.
